{"id":"iceland-highlands-4x4","title":"Iceland's Highlands by 4x4","who":"Classic route · the F-roads of the interior","when":"Late June/July to early September, when the F-roads open","vehicle":"4x4 (required by law), 7–10 days","kind":"4x4","color":"#334155","summary":"Through the empty interior on the summer-only F-roads: the coloured rhyolite hills and hot river of Landmannalaugar, the black desert of Sprengisandur between two ice caps, Askja's crater lakes, and the geothermal valley of Hveravellir on the Kjölur road. River crossings, no fuel, no shops: check road.is and your rental insurance.","sources":[{"label":"Guide to Iceland: F-roads, a guide to Icelandic mountain roads","url":"https://guidetoiceland.is/best-of-iceland/f-roads-in-iceland-a-guide-to-icelandic-mountain-roads"},{"label":"Luxe Adventure Traveler: 9-day Iceland Highlands 4x4 itinerary","url":"https://luxeadventuretraveler.com/iceland-highlands-itinerary-the-ultimate-9-day-4x4-adventure/"}],"approximate":"Main stops; the F-roads are drawn as straight lines where the routers don't know them.","km":900,"bbox":[-21.9429,63.879,-15.8404,65.6605],"stops":[{"name":"Reykjavík","place":"Reykjavík, Iceland","at":[64.146,-21.9422],"text":"Pick up the 4x4 and supplies.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Reykjav%C3%ADk%2C_view_from_Hallgr%C3%ADmskirkja_%282%29.jpg/500px-Reykjav%C3%ADk%2C_view_from_Hallgr%C3%ADmskirkja_%282%29.jpg","page":"Reykjavík","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reykjav%C3%ADk%2C_view_from_Hallgr%C3%ADmskirkja_%282%29.jpg","credit":"Olga Ernst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Landmannalaugar","place":"Landmannalaugar","at":[63.9917,-19.0606],"text":"Rhyolite mountains in every colour and a natural hot stream.","source":{"label":"Guide to Iceland","url":"https://guidetoiceland.is/best-of-iceland/f-roads-in-iceland-a-guide-to-icelandic-mountain-roads"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Landmannalaugar_Campsite.jpg/500px-Landmannalaugar_Campsite.jpg","page":"Landmannalaugar","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Landmannalaugar_Campsite.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Hrauneyjar","place":"Hrauneyjar","at":[64.1972,-19.2706],"text":"The last fuel before the interior.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Sprengisandur-location.png/500px-Sprengisandur-location.png","page":"Sprengisandur","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sprengisandur-location.png","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Sprengisandur","place":"Nýidalur","at":[64.7353,-18.0711],"text":"About 200 km of black desert between Hofsjökull and Vatnajökull.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Sprengisandur-location.png/500px-Sprengisandur-location.png","page":"Sprengisandur","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sprengisandur-location.png","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Askja","place":"Askja","at":[65.0525,-16.7764],"text":"A caldera with the milky-blue Víti crater lake.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Askja.jpg/500px-Askja.jpg","page":"Askja","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Askja.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Mývatn","place":"Reykjahlíð, Iceland","at":[65.6416,-16.91],"text":"Out to Lake Mývatn and its nature baths.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/M%C3%BDvatn-pjt.jpg/500px-M%C3%BDvatn-pjt.jpg","page":"Mývatn","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%BDvatn-pjt.jpg","credit":"Pjt56 --- If you use the picture outside Wikipedia I would appreciate a short e-mail to pjt56@gmx.net or a message on my","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Hveravellir","place":"Hveravellir","at":[64.8664,-19.5544],"text":"Back south on the Kjölur road to a